# core.autocrlf is on for this machine, so without this every file would be
# checked out with CRLF -- while build.py, the tools and the deploy script
# all write LF (io.open(..., newline="\n")). The two would disagree on every
# line of every file, and each build would look like a rewrite of the whole
# tree. Pin LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# It matters beyond noise for two of these: web/.htaccess and
# guide/build-guide.sh are read by Apache and /bin/sh on the server, and a
# CRLF copy of either fails there and not here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never translate these. The figures are the bulk of the
# repo and most are photographs or scans.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.JPG  binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# SVG is text and diffs usefully, so it is deliberately not listed above.
